      "extract": "The notion of the *semisimplification* of a spherical tensor category was introduced in [@BW], although in the context of algebraic geometry it can be traced back to the notion of numerical equivalence of cycles in the theory of motives, see e.g. [@Ja]. More generally, various *adequate equivalence relations* in the same theory can be considered as examples of *tensor ideals* in the symmetric tensor category of Chow",
